<newsitem itemid="92345" id="root" date="1996-10-02" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Bank of Scotland raises pre-tax profits.</title>
<headline>Bank of Scotland raises pre-tax profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-year to August 31</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  15.0		 vs 12.6</p>
<p> Dividend  (pence)	  2.91		 vs 2.45</p>
<p> Pretax			 324.3		vs 261.6</p>
<p> Pre-provision profit     408.2		vs 339.6</p>
<p> Cost/income ratio	  52.9		 vs 50.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 283 to 305 million stg.  </p>
<p> Bad/doubtful debt charge 70.2		 vs 65.3</p>
<p> Tax			    119.5		vs 98.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		    204.8		vs 163.1</p>
<p> Net interest income	606.0		vs 460.0</p>
<p> Fees and commissions     280.2		vs 218.8</p>
<p> Net operating income     870.5		vs 665.7</p>
<p> Admin expenses	     425.8		vs 318.7</p>
<p> Profit on disposal	 nil		  vs 23.6</p>
<p> Attributable		 191.7		vs 161.5</p>
<p> Pay date		     November 29</p>
<p> Div registration date    October 22</p>
<p> Ex-div date		  October 14</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
